WEBVTT

00:00:02.259 --> 00:00:08.009
Tess?

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:09.630
Um...

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:13.839
You didn't have to come all the way out here.

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:15.460
There's caffeine dealers in Metropolis.

00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:18.660
I just...

00:00:18.660 --> 00:00:21.480
I just feel like you and I haven't had a chance

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.780
to really catch up lately.

00:00:24.989 --> 00:00:25.370
Okay.

00:00:25.929 --> 00:00:29.059
So how are you?

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:30.219
Good. Good.

00:00:30.899 --> 00:00:31.620
How are you?

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:33.899
I'm fine, thanks.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.020
Right.

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:38.840
Okay.

00:00:39.119 --> 00:00:45.570
Uh, it's just that there has been a little incident

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:47.070
with our little project.

00:00:47.270 --> 00:00:47.729
What happened?

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:52.450
Um, ever since Alexander's reboot,

00:00:52.549 --> 00:00:54.270
he has been totally glitch-free

00:00:54.270 --> 00:00:56.570
and ready to enter the real world.

00:00:57.289 --> 00:01:01.210
Except he needs, he needs someone to guide him.

00:01:02.469 --> 00:01:04.709
Um, someone like you.

00:01:06.489 --> 00:01:06.769
Me?

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:12.189
He's a genetically engineered version of Lex.

00:01:12.189 --> 00:01:13.969
I don't think I'd be the best mentor for him.

00:01:14.969 --> 00:01:15.769
About that.

00:01:16.489 --> 00:01:19.530
He's soaking up new information like an MIT grad.

00:01:19.530 --> 00:01:20.609
And I think, I think he's,

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:24.049
He just needs someone there for him, like family.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:27.170
Well, technically, you are his sister.

00:01:28.909 --> 00:01:29.890
But I'm no Clark Kent.

00:01:31.150 --> 00:01:34.090
I know you are the one that can bring out the best in him.

00:01:37.079 --> 00:01:39.420
Which is why he is outside waiting in the car.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:41.459
Here?

00:01:42.959 --> 00:01:44.359
Tess, you shouldn't...

00:01:44.359 --> 00:01:45.799
What if you remember something about me?

00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:47.299
He doesn't. He doesn't remember anything

00:01:47.299 --> 00:01:49.480
because he's going through this sort of metamorphosis.

00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:50.819
And ever since he's been changing,

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:52.540
we have been learning new things about him.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:56.739
like things about his, um, genetic origin.

00:01:57.340 --> 00:02:15.560
The test.

00:02:16.219 --> 00:02:16.979
Check it out.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.919
Um, he doesn't just have Lex's genes.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.400
Half his DNA came from you.

00:03:48.729 --> 00:03:51.129
It's not just the Luther males who like secrets.

00:03:51.669 --> 00:03:54.129
Given the fact that you're here, this place isn't really much of a secret.

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.289
Ah, yeah, but you're forgetting.

00:03:57.530 --> 00:03:59.129
I'm running Luther Corp now.

00:04:00.090 --> 00:04:04.789
One of my, uh, crackerjack accountants informed me that millions of dollars have been funneled.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:10.090
into this facility, but, uh, it looks as if you've closed up shop.

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:17.579
I applaud your efforts, but you can't hide Alexander from me forever.

00:04:17.579 --> 00:04:21.660
I'm saving him from an encore performance of Daddy Dearest.

00:04:22.220 --> 00:04:23.740
Give me my son.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:29.100
I'm surprised you are so hell-bent on this family reunion, given the fact that in this world,

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.620
it was Lex that sent Lionel plummeting to his death.

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.620
That's proof that the Lex you knew was a true Luther.

00:04:36.860 --> 00:04:43.149
I made a terrible mistake, Tess.

00:04:44.670 --> 00:04:49.810
I should never have trusted Clark, more than my own flesh and blood.

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:59.730
Considering what happened to me, I'd say that turning your back on your own is the dominant Luther trait.

00:05:00.769 --> 00:05:04.230
Which is why the Luther legacy ends with you.

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:08.149
Tess?

00:05:11.399 --> 00:05:11.899
Yeah.

00:05:16.389 --> 00:05:21.589
If I'd been your father, when Lionel gave you up for adoption, I would have done precisely.

00:05:22.189 --> 00:05:25.500
I would have done precisely.

00:05:25.519 --> 00:05:27.519
as he did.

00:05:27.519 --> 00:05:28.519
Why?

00:05:28.519 --> 00:05:31.519
Because you can't control me?

00:05:31.519 --> 00:05:32.519
No.

00:05:32.519 --> 00:05:35.519
Because you are inferior.

00:05:35.519 --> 00:05:42.500
Imagine what a boy like Alexander could do if he had the right guidance.

00:05:42.500 --> 00:05:50.639
You're right.

00:05:50.639 --> 00:05:57.240
Come with me.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:06:07.370
Your son is in there.

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:15.629
We couldn't find a cure to stop the accelerated mitosis.

00:06:15.629 --> 00:06:20.759
You're lying.

00:06:20.759 --> 00:06:22.759
I don't believe you.

00:06:22.759 --> 00:06:24.759
There are enough bone chips in those that.

00:06:24.759 --> 00:06:26.759
ashes for a DNA test.

00:06:26.759 --> 00:06:29.759
That will prove that I'm telling the truth.

00:06:29.759 --> 00:06:38.069
Your son is dead, final.

00:06:38.069 --> 00:06:40.069
You'll never be able to hurt him again.

00:06:40.069 --> 00:06:56.720
Thanks for your help.

00:06:56.720 --> 00:06:59.720
You're the one hiding a mutant under your roof.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:02.720
Tuss keeps me on the move.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:06.720
This is a hundred times about in the playing lab rat for a bunch of doctors.

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:09.720
They think I can't hear what they say about me.

00:07:09.720 --> 00:07:15.209
So your name is Connor?

00:07:15.209 --> 00:07:17.209
It's from my medical files.

00:07:17.209 --> 00:07:21.209
C&R, Conner.

00:07:21.209 --> 00:07:24.209
Tess thinks she's kept out a big secret from me.

00:07:24.209 --> 00:07:27.209
I think she's just embarrassed, you know,

00:07:27.209 --> 00:07:29.209
taking care of a walking freak show.

00:07:29.209 --> 00:07:31.209
She doesn't think that way.

00:07:31.209 --> 00:07:34.209
I promise. She's trying to protect you.

00:07:34.209 --> 00:07:38.209
How people would react if they found out what I really was?

00:07:38.209 --> 00:07:41.209
You'd be surprised how much it doesn't matter when people get to know you.

00:07:41.209 --> 00:07:46.100
That's really PC of you, but

00:07:46.100 --> 00:07:48.100
you don't understand what it feels like.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:49.100
Every time you meet someone new,

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:54.100
some new doctor if they're going to hate you just for who you are,

00:07:54.100 --> 00:07:57.100
or maybe even be jealous that they can't do what you can do.

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:03.079
Is it true you can't remember anything from before you got your abilities?

00:08:03.079 --> 00:08:06.079
Zip. Mutation's a bitch.

00:08:06.079 --> 00:08:11.779
Honestly, I understand Tess is trying to protect me from a whole bunch of stuff,

00:08:11.779 --> 00:08:15.779
but I need to find out where I come from.

00:08:15.779 --> 00:08:17.779
Why I am the way I am.

00:08:17.779 --> 00:08:23.310
I'm sure she'll tell you when you're ready.

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:24.310
I'm ready now.

00:08:24.310 --> 00:08:25.310
I'm ready now.

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:32.309
No disrespect, but I can't stand around here milking cows when there's so much I need to know.

00:08:32.309 --> 00:08:38.379
Appreciate your hospitality, but...

00:08:38.379 --> 00:08:39.379
You're not leaving.

00:08:39.379 --> 00:08:43.590
That almost sounded like it wasn't a question.

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:50.120
Look, it's important to test that you stick around here for a while.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:53.120
And it's important to me that I find out who and what I really am.

00:08:53.120 --> 00:08:55.120
What if someone catches on to the fact that you're different?

00:08:55.120 --> 00:09:02.799
I can't let you take that risk. I'm sorry.

00:09:02.799 --> 00:09:05.799
Sorry, but it's my risk to take.

00:09:05.799 --> 00:09:06.799
Besides,

00:09:06.799 --> 00:09:08.799
you can't exactly stop me.

00:09:08.799 --> 00:09:18.860
You're...

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:22.559
I'm like you.

00:09:22.559 --> 00:09:24.559
So does this mean...

00:09:24.559 --> 00:09:28.559
Oh my God. Are you like my dad?

00:09:28.559 --> 00:09:31.559
I prefer brother.

00:09:31.559 --> 00:09:33.559
I thought I was the only one with these powers.

00:09:33.559 --> 00:09:36.559
Well, me and the blur.

00:09:36.559 --> 00:09:38.559
Wait.

00:09:38.559 --> 00:09:39.559
Are you...

00:09:39.559 --> 00:09:41.559
Are you him?

00:09:41.559 --> 00:09:44.480
The blur?

00:09:44.480 --> 00:09:46.480
How do you know about the blur?

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:47.480
Are you kidding me?

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:48.480
I've read about every...

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.480
save he's made, or you've made.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:53.480
Well, come on, let's go to Metropolis and save somebody together.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:55.480
Wait, you have still some things you need to learn.

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:57.480
All I've been doing is learning.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:09:59.480
I want to do something.

00:09:59.480 --> 00:10:01.480
Yeah, it's exciting to have no abilities.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.480
But you need to learn how to control them.

00:10:03.480 --> 00:10:07.480
We're going to stay here on the farm and practice.

00:10:07.480 --> 00:10:10.480
Come on. I don't need to practice.

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:12.480
Trust me. I'm in total control.

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:13.480
Clark!

00:10:13.480 --> 00:10:18.009
What the hell I've been trying to call you?

00:10:18.009 --> 00:10:21.419
Uh, Lois. This is my...

00:10:21.419 --> 00:10:22.419
My friend Connor.

00:10:22.419 --> 00:10:25.419
Connor, this is my fiancée Loessling.

00:10:25.419 --> 00:10:28.370
Hi.

00:10:28.370 --> 00:10:31.370
I need you to sign off on the by-life by noon

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:33.370
